== [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")])","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call has a tracker of its own, so tests running at the same time never see each other’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events. The body may be sync or async, and may return a value, read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.value"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.names"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every event’s name and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.records"},{"type":"text","text":" every record."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most code needs nothing more: it tracks through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.current"},{"type":"text","text":", which falls back to the tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app bootstrapped, and the test’s binding wins over that one. A view whose tracker was never set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that binds its tracker with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" reaches the test’s tracker too. Pass a tracker instead where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"code reads one set for a single view tree. A tracker given to a SwiftUI view with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", such as a preview’s,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches the view’s environment but not code that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.current"},{"type":"text","text":". Such a test takes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker the body is given and sets it on the view: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker { tracker in … }"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"type":"topic","url":